The image is a lateral chest X-ray. In a standard lateral view, the patient's left side is typically closer to the detector (or the orientation marker indicates the side). However, determining "left" vs "right" breast on a single lateral view without explicit markers can be tricky, but usually, the anterior soft tissue shadow corresponds to the breast. The question asks about surgical instruments. I need to look for radiopaque linear densities within the breast shadow.

Let's use `chest_xray_expert` to get a focused interpretation of the breast area and any foreign bodies.

{"calls":[{"tool":"chest_xray_expert","args":{"question":"Are there surgical instruments or foreign bodies in the breast shadow? If so, which side (left or right) based on lateral view conventions?"}}],"reason":"Identify presence and location of surgical instruments in breast shadow."}

